<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick I, Landgrave of Hesse-Homburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1585">1585</a>–<a href="/years/1638">1638</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick I was the youngest son of Landgrave George I of Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a>. In 1622 his brother Louis V granted him Homburg vor der Höhe as an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a>, making him the first landgrave of Hesse-Homburg, a branch that stayed dependent on Hesse-Darmstadt for most of its history. His descendants ruled Homburg until the line died out in 1866.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-i-landgrave-of-hesse-homburg.jpg" alt="Frederick I, Landgrave of Hesse-Homburg" width="300" height="380" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hessen%C5%A1ki_de%C5%BEelni_grof_Friederich_III._(sr._17._st.).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
